<header><p class="enc-kicker">Event</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anschluss</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1938</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anschluss was the annexation of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austria">Austria</a> by Nazi <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> in March 1938. After Chancellor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kurt-schuschnigg">Kurt Schuschnigg</a> called a referendum on independence, Hitler forced his resignation, and German troops crossed the border on 12 March to an enthusiastic reception from many Austrians. A plebiscite held under Nazi control in April recorded over 99 per cent approval. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a> declared the annexation void in 1943, and Austria was restored as a separate state in 1945.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anschluss.jpg" alt="Anschluss" width="320" height="443" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Heinrich Hoffmann · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Anschluss_Heldenplatz1.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
